# Bypass of LineageSetupWizard (diagnostics 18.09.2026, see docs/findings.md):
# excluding the package from the build (PRODUCT_PACKAGES := $(filter-out ...)) failed —
# the entry is re-added at a later stage of product processing, so filter-out
# in the top-level .mk does not work here. Instead we programmatically do the same thing
# the wizard itself does on completion (disableHome() in SetupWizardUtils.java) —
# but earlier than the user could go through it interactively.
#
# seclabel u:r:shell:s0 is required (NOT u:r:system_app:s0 — that domain lacks
# permissions for the binder calls pm needs, it fails with SecurityException/segfault).
# user system is required (NOT shell — adb shell gets SecurityException:
# "Shell cannot change component state", a UID check in
# PackageManagerService, not by SELinux domain). The file /bin/wsa-no-setupwizard.sh itself
# must carry the label u:object_r:shell_exec:s0 (not the generic system
# system_file) — the shell domain enters the process only through an entrypoint of this
# type.
service wsa_no_setupwizard /system_ext/bin/wsa-no-setupwizard.sh
    class late_start
    user system
    group system
    oneshot
    disabled
    seclabel u:r:shell:s0

# Settings — as uid shell: on Android 16 `settings put` as uid system crashes (NPE in
# AppOpsService.checkPackage), see the script itself.
service wsa_settings /system_ext/bin/wsa-no-setupwizard.sh settings
    class late_start
    user shell
    group shell
    oneshot
    disabled
    seclabel u:r:shell:s0

on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    start wsa_no_setupwizard
    start wsa_settings

# userdebug: init starts the `console` shell on the serial port (ro.debuggable=1), and
# ActivityManager posts a persistent "Serial console enabled" notification — it
# ends up in the Windows notification center (30.09.2026, aosp16-vanilla). We read the kernel console from the host
# (bin/wsa-guest-console.sh), no shell on the port is needed; Microsoft stock (a user build) does not have it.
on property:init.svc.console=running
    stop console
